    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d354">

                <pb facs="0523" n="403" sameAs="frus:frus1905/pg403"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        Minister Dawson.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1905-11-04"><hi rendition="#italic">November 4,
                        1905</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>There appears to be conflict of procedure between American naval officers
                    boarding vessels for the purpose of ascertaining whether they are importing arms
                    and ammunition in violation of President’s proclamation of October 14 and
                    customs authorities at Monte Christi, who insist upon their right to board first
                    under regulations. Request decision of question by Dominican Government. If they
                    wish effective prevention of importation arms and ammunition, port regulations
                    should be modified to make boarding and search of American ships by naval
                    officers acting in behalf of Dominican Government unquestionably lawful. If they
                    wish naval officers to desist from such boarding and search, this government
                    will instruct accordingly. Confer with Dominican Government as to moral effect
                    of discontinuing present practice. We have some apprehension that it would
                    encourage would-be revolutionists.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Root.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
